[0.000, "o", "                       \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m \u001b[38;2;128;128;128m/Users/badlogic/workspaces/pi-mono/packages/coding-agent/src/core/compaction.ts:27:               \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m \u001b[38;2;128;128;128mkeepRecentTokens: 20000,\u001b[39m                                                                          \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m \u001b[38;2;128;128;128m/Users/badlogic/workspaces/pi-mono/packages/coding-agent/src/core/compaction.ts:75:   return      \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m \u001b[38;2;128;128;128mcontextTokens > contextWindow - settings.reserveTokens;\u001b[39m\u001b[38;2;128;128;128m                                           \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m ... (19 more lines)\u001b[39m                                                                               \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m                                                                                                   \u001b[49m\r\r\n\r\r\n Here's a summary of how compaction works:                                                         \r\r\n                                        "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                           \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;240;198;116m\u001b[1mCompaction Overview\u001b[22m\u001b[39m                                                                               \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[1mTrigger conditions:\u001b[22m                                                                               \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m1. \u001b[39m\u001b[1mThreshold\u001b[22m: After each turn, if \u001b[38;2;138;190;183mcontextTokens > contextWindow - reserveTokens\u001b[39m, compaction runs  \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m2. \u001b[39m\u001b[1mOverflow\u001b[22m: If the LLM returns a context overflow error, compaction runs and retries             \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[1mKey settings (defaults):\u001b[22m                                                                          \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m- \u001b[39m\u001b[38;2;138;190;183mreserveTokens: 16384\u001b[39m - Buffer to leave for new responses"]
[0.000, "o", "                                        \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m- \u001b[39m\u001b[38;2;138;190;183mkeepRecentTokens: 20000\u001b[39m - How many tokens of recent messages to keep                            \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[1mmaxTokens usage:\u001b[22m                                                                                  \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mFor summarization\u001b[22m: \u001b[38;2;138;190;183mmaxTokens = 0.8 * reserveTokens\u001b[39m (≈13,107 tokens)                             \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m- \u001b[39m\u001b[1mFor turn prefix summary\u001b[22m: \u001b[38;2;138;190;183mmaxTokens = 0.5 * reserveTokens\u001b[39m (≈8,192 tokens)                        \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[1mThe process:\u001b[22m                                                                                      \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m1. \u001b[39mFind the cut point by walking backwards from newest mes"]
[0.000, "o", "sages until \u001b[38;2;138;190;183mkeepRecentTokens\u001b[39m is         \r\r\n accumulated                                                                                       \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m2. \u001b[39mGenerate a summary of everything before the cut point                                          \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m3. \u001b[39mIf cutting mid-turn (at an assistant message), also generate a \"turn prefix summary\"           \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m4. \u001b[39mSave a \u001b[38;2;138;190;183mCompactionEntry\u001b[39m with the summary and \u001b[38;2;138;190;183mfirstKeptEntryIndex\u001b[39m                                \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m5. \u001b[39mOn session reload, messages before \u001b[38;2;138;190;183mfirstKeptEntryIndex\u001b[39m are replaced with the summary           \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[1mSo yes, maxTokens IS set\u001b[22m for the summarization LLM calls, but there's no explicit maxTokens for   \r\r\n the main agent's responses. The compaction system relies on:     "]
[0.000, "o", "                                 \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m- \u001b[39mThe model's \u001b[38;2;138;190;183mcontextWindow\u001b[39m property (from model definition)                                      \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m- \u001b[39m\u001b[38;2;138;190;183mreserveTokens\u001b[39m buffer to leave headroom                                                          \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m- \u001b[39mToken counts from \u001b[38;2;138;190;183musage\u001b[39m in assistant responses                                                  \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;52;53;65m                                                                                                   \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;52;53;65m \u001b[39mwe have fixtures in coding-agent for compaction, don'T read them in full, they are huge. in any   \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;52;53;65m case, i'd like to experiment with compaction a little. we already do 2 calls to summarize, one    \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;52;53;65m for history, one for turn prefix. i wonder if we could get more bang for the bug if we:\u001b[39m           \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;52;53;65m                 "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                                                  \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;52;53;65m \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m- \u001b[39m\u001b[39msegmented the session into slices (possibly overlapping)\u001b[39m                                        \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;52;53;65m \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m- \u001b[39m\u001b[39msummarized each slice with a summary token budget that's 1/10th of the slice size\u001b[39m               \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;52;53;65m \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m- \u001b[39m\u001b[39mstitched those slice summaries together into a single summary\u001b[39m                                   \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;52;53;65m                                                                                                   \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;52;53;65m \u001b[39mi'd also like to explore the summrization prompt of claude code. for that, we can download its    \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;52;53;65m npm package and search cli.js (huge js fiel, don't try to read at once)\u001b[39m                           \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;52;53;65m                                                                    "]
