[0.000, "o", "                                               \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;240;198;116m\u001b[1m### Your Slice-Based Idea\u001b[22m\u001b[39m                                                                         \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n The concept: segment session into slices, summarize each with budget = 1/10th of slice size, then \r\r\n stitch together.                                                                                  \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n This could work well because:                                                                     \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m1. \u001b[39mMore parallelizable (summarize slices concurrently)                                            \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m2. \u001b[39mLess risk of losing detail in long sessions                              "]
[0.000, "o", "                      \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m3. \u001b[39mBetter \"compression ratio\" awareness per slice                                                 \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m4. \u001b[39mCan handle overlapping slices for continuity                                                   \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n Want me to prototype this slice-based approach?                                                   \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;52;53;65m                                                                                                   \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;52;53;65m \u001b[39mcan you also dry to find droid's summary prompt? which droid, and see if it is actually           \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;52;53;65m javascript as well. finally, you could check the summary prompt of                                \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;52;53;65m \u001b[39m\u001b[38;2;129;162;190m\u001b[4m\u001b[39mhttps://github.com/openai/codex/issues\u001b[39m\u001b[24m\u001b[39m\u001b[39m                                                          "]
