[0.000, "o", "      \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m                                                                                                   \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m \u001b[38;2;128;128;128m/tmp/openai-codex/codex-rs/core/gpt_5_codex_prompt.md:68:- If the user asks for a \"review\",       \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m \u001b[38;2;128;128;128mdefault to a code review mindset: prioritise identifying bugs, risks, behavioural regressions,    \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m \u001b[38;2;128;128;128mand missing tests. Findings must be the primary focus of the response - keep summaries or         \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m \u001b[38;2;128;128;128moverviews brief and only after enumerating the issues. Present findings first (ordered by         \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m \u001b[38;2;128;128;128mseverity with file/line references), follow with open questions or assumptions, and offer a       \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m \u001b[38;2;128;128;128mchange-summary only as a secondary detail. If no findings are discovered, state that explicitly   \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m \u001b[38;2;128;128;128"]
