[0.000, "o", ";50;40m \u001b[38;2;128;128;128m### Settings (defaults)\u001b[39m                                                                           \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m \u001b[38;2;128;128;128m- `reserveTokens: 16384` - Buffer to leave for new responses\u001b[39m                                      \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m \u001b[38;2;128;128;128m- `keepRecentTokens: 20000` - How many tokens of recent messages to keep\u001b[39m                          \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m \u001b[38;2;128;128;128m\u001b[39m                                                                                                  \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m \u001b[38;2;128;128;128m### Trigger Conditions\u001b[39m                                                                            \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m \u001b[38;2;128;128;128m1. **Threshold**: After each turn, if `contextTokens > contextWindow - reserveTokens`\u001b[39m\u001b[38;2;128;128;128m             \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;40;50;40m ... (341 more lines)\u001b[39m                                                                              \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48"]
[0.000, "o", ";2;40;50;40m                                                                                                   \u001b[49m\r\r\n\r\r\n Created \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m/Users/badlogic/workspaces/pi-mono/packages/coding-agent/compaction-new.md\u001b[39m with:          \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m1. \u001b[39m\u001b[1mCurrent Pi implementation\u001b[22m details                                                              \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m2. \u001b[39m\u001b[1mClaude Code's approach\u001b[22m - full reconstructed prompt with 9-section structured format and        \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m<analysis>\u001b[39m/\u001b[38;2;138;190;183m<summary>\u001b[39m tags                                                                         \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m3. \u001b[39m\u001b[1mOpenAI Codex's approach\u001b[22m - their simple prompt plus summary prefix for continuity               \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m4. \u001b[39m\u001b[1mSST OpenCode's approach\u001b[22m - compaction + pruning system (marks old tool outputs as c"]
[0.000, "o", "ompacted     \r\r\n after 40K tokens)                                                                                 \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m5. \u001b[39m\u001b[1mFactory Droid\u001b[22m - scratchpad feature that persists across compaction                             \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m6. \u001b[39m\u001b[1mProposed slice-based algorithm\u001b[22m with example code and prompts                                   \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m7. \u001b[39m\u001b[1mComparison table\u001b[22m and \u001b[1mrecommendations\u001b[22m                                                           \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n Key findings:                                                                                     \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m- \u001b[39mClaude Code has the most sophisticated prompt (structured sections, chain-of-thought)           \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m- \u001b[39mOpenCode has an interesting pruning mechanism (compacts old tool outputs in-place)              \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m- \u001b[39mDroid has"]
[0.000, "o", " a \"scratchpad\" concept for persistent working memory                                  \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m- \u001b[39mNobody does parallel slice-based summarization yet                                              \r\r\n\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;52;53;65m                                                                                                   \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;52;53;65m \u001b[39mcan you describe how concretely such a slice based summarization could work?\u001b[39m                      \u001b[49m\r\r\n\u001b[48;2;52;53;65m                                                                                                   \u001b[49m\r\r\n\r\r\n \u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;128;128;128mThe user wants me to think through and describe in more detail how slice-based summarization      \r\r\n \u001b[3;38;2;128;128;128mwould actually work in practice. Let me think through this concretely:\u001b[39m\u001b[23m                            \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m1. \u001b[39m\u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;128;128;128mHow do we se"]
[0.000, "o", "gment messages into slices?\u001b[39m\u001b[23m                                                        \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m2. \u001b[39m\u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;128;128;128mHow do we handle overlap?\u001b[39m\u001b[23m                                                                      \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m3. \u001b[39m\u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;128;128;128mWhat's the actual flow?\u001b[39m\u001b[23m                                                                        \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m4. \u001b[39m\u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;128;128;128mHow do we stitch summaries together?\u001b[39m\u001b[23m                                                           \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m5. \u001b[39m\u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;128;128;128mWhat are the edge cases?\u001b[39m\u001b[23m                                                                       \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[3m\u001b[38;2;128;128;128mLet me think through this step by step with concrete examples.\u001b[39m\u001b[23m                                    \r\r\n\r\r\n Let me think through this concretely with an exampl"]
[0.000, "o", "e scenario.                                    \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;240;198;116m\u001b[1mSlice-Based Summarization: Concrete Design\u001b[22m\u001b[39m                                                        \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;240;198;116m\u001b[1m### Scenario\u001b[22m\u001b[39m                                                                                      \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n Session with ~200K tokens of history, need to compact to ~20K summary.                            \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;240;198;116m\u001b[1m### Step 1: Segmentation\u001b[22m\u001b[39m                                                                          \r\r\n                                                           "]
[0.000, "o", "                                        \r\r\n Walk through messages and create slices at \u001b[1mturn boundaries\u001b[22m (user message starts). Each slice      \r\r\n targets ~30K tokens with ~5K overlap.                                                             \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;128;128;128m```\u001b[39m                                                                                               \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104mMessages: [u1, a1, u2, a2, u3, a3, u4, a4, u5, a5, u6, a6, u7, a7]\u001b[39m                              \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m           |-------- slice 0 --------|\u001b[39m                                                          \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m                          |-------- slice 1 --------|\u001b[39m                                           \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m                                         |-------- slice 2 --------|\u001b[39m                            \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m              "]
[0.000, "o", "                                          |-- slice 3 (recent) --|\u001b[39m                \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;128;128;128m```\u001b[39m                                                                                               \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n The overlap ensures context carries across boundaries. We never cut in the middle of a turn (user \r\r\n + assistant response).                                                                            \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;240;198;116m\u001b[1m### Step 2: Estimate & Budget\u001b[22m\u001b[39m                                                                     \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;128;128;128m```typescript\u001b[39m                       "]
[0.000, "o", "                                                              \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m// Example with 200K total tokens\u001b[39m                                                               \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104mconst slices = [\u001b[39m                                                                                \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m  { messages: [...], tokens: 32000 },  // slice 0: early work\u001b[39m                                   \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m  { messages: [...], tokens: 35000 },  // slice 1: middle  \u001b[39m                                     \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m  { messages: [...], tokens: 33000 },  // slice 2: middle-recent\u001b[39m                                \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m  { messages: [...], tokens: 25000 },  // slice 3: most recent\u001b[39m                                  \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m];\u001b[39m                                                                                              \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m\u001b[39m                                                  "]
[0.000, "o", "                                              \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m// Compression ratio: 1/10 base, 1/5 for recent\u001b[39m                                                 \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104mconst budgets = [\u001b[39m                                                                               \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m  3200,   // slice 0: 32K * 0.10\u001b[39m                                                                \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m  3500,   // slice 1: 35K * 0.10\u001b[39m                                                                \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m  3300,   // slice 2: 33K * 0.10\u001b[39m                                                                \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m  5000,   // slice 3: 25K * 0.20 (boosted - most recent)\u001b[39m                                        \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m];\u001b[39m                                                                                              \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m// Total: ~15K tokens for summaries\u001b[39m                               "]
[0.000, "o", "                              \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;128;128;128m```\u001b[39m                                                                                               \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;240;198;116m\u001b[1m### Step 3: Parallel Summarization\u001b[22m\u001b[39m                                                                \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n Fire off all slice summarizations concurrently:                                                   \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;128;128;128m```typescript\u001b[39m                                                                                     \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104mconst sliceSummaries = await Promise.all(\u001b[39m                          "]
[0.000, "o", "                             \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m  slices.map((slice, i) => \u001b[39m                                                                     \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m    summarizeSlice({\u001b[39m                                                                            \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m      messages: slice.messages,\u001b[39m                                                                 \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m      sliceIndex: i,\u001b[39m                                                                            \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m      totalSlices: slices.length,\u001b[39m                                                               \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m      maxTokens: budgets[i],\u001b[39m                                                                    \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m      isFirst: i === 0,\u001b[39m                                                                         \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m      isLast: i === slices.length - 1,\u001b[39m                                             "]
[0.000, "o", "             \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m    })\u001b[39m                                                                                          \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m  )\u001b[39m                                                                                             \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m);\u001b[39m                                                                                              \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;128;128;128m```\u001b[39m                                                                                               \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;240;198;116m\u001b[1m### Step 4: Slice-Specific Prompts\u001b[22m\u001b[39m                                                                \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[1mFor early slices (0, 1):\u001b[22m                             "]
[0.000, "o", "                                             \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;128;128;128m```\u001b[39m                                                                                               \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104mSummarize this segment of a coding session (segment 1 of 4).\u001b[39m                                    \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m\u001b[39m                                                                                                \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104mFocus on:\u001b[39m                                                                                       \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m- Initial user goals and requirements established\u001b[39m                                               \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m- Key architectural decisions made\u001b[39m                                                              \r\r\n   \u001b[38;2;181;189;104m- Files created or significantly modified\u001b[39m                                                  "]
