[0.000, "o", "                                                      \r\r\n It implements 4 strategies:                                                                       \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m1. \u001b[39m\u001b[1msingle-shot\u001b[22m - Current approach (one big call)                                                  \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m2. \u001b[39m\u001b[1mparallel-stitch\u001b[22m - Parallel slice summaries → LLM merge                                         \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m3. \u001b[39m\u001b[1msequential-accumulated\u001b[22m - Each slice gets all previous slice summaries as context               \r\r\n \u001b[38;2;138;190;183m4. \u001b[39m\u001b[1msequential-rolling\u001b[22m - Each call updates the running summary (what you didn't want)              \r\r\n                                                                                                   \r\r\n Results go to \u001b[38;2;138;190;183mtest/compaction-results/\u001b[39m as markdown files for easy comparison.                 "]
